Report entry names of any length in inotifyd on Windows.
The name of the changed entry was converted into a buffer of MAX_PATH
bytes. A name that converted to exactly MAX_PATH bytes filled it with
no room for a terminator, so it was printed or passed to the agent with
stray bytes from the stack after it. A longer name, possible since one
UTF-16 unit can take up to three bytes in a multibyte code page such as
UTF-8, made the conversion fail and was reported with no name at all.

Ask WideCharToMultiByte for the converted length first and allocate a
buffer one byte larger.

---
 miscutils/inotifyd.c |   10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/miscutils/inotifyd.c
+++ b/miscutils/inotifyd.c
@@ -271,14 +271,15 @@
 						struct watch *w)
 {
 	int len;
-	char filename[MAX_PATH];
+	char *filename;
 	char event[2];
 	const char *args[5];
 
-	memset(filename, 0, sizeof(filename));
 	len = WideCharToMultiByte(CP_ACP, 0, info->FileName,
-				info->FileNameLength/2, filename, sizeof(filename),
-				NULL, NULL);
+				info->FileNameLength/2, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
+	filename = xzalloc(len + 1);
+	WideCharToMultiByte(CP_ACP, 0, info->FileName,
+				info->FileNameLength/2, filename, len, NULL, NULL);
 
 	if (info->Action >= 0 && info->Action < 6 &&
 				((1 << info->Action) & w->bits)) {
@@ -300,6 +301,7 @@
 			spawn_and_wait((char **)args);
 		}
 	}
+	free(filename);
 }
 
 static BOOL start_watch(struct watch *w)
